---
import '../styles/global.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Dartpollo documentation: generate typed Dart models from GraphQL and execute them with caching, streaming, and cancellation." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${base}/favicon.svg`} />
    <title>Dartpollo Docs — Typed GraphQL for Dart</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <!--
      DIRECTION: Typed field guide
      MODE: Read — developers should understand the schema-to-response path immediately.
      WORLD: Technical field notes with connected specimens and precise code typography.
      SIGNATURE: A vertical GraphQL pipeline turns schema, query, generated type, and response into one visible system.
      RESPONSIVE: The split field guide becomes a single connected reading path on small screens.
    -->
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to documentation</a>
    <header class="topbar">
      <div class="topbar-inner">
        <a class="brand" href={base} aria-label="Dartpollo documentation home">
          <img class="brand-mark" src={`${base}/favicon.svg`} alt="" />
          <span>Dartpollo</span>
          <span class="version">v0.1.0-alpha.6</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary navigation">
          <a href="#quickstart">Quickstart</a>
          <a href="#caching">Caching</a>
          <a href="https://pub.dev/packages/dartpollo">pub.dev</a>
          <a class="github-link" href="https://github.com/dwikyhardi/dartpollo">GitHub ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-inner">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <h1>GraphQL in. <span>Typed Dart</span> out.</h1>
            <p>Dartpollo generates Dart models from your schema and operations, then executes them through a focused client with caching, streaming, and cancellation built in.</p>
            <div class="actions">
              <a class="button primary" href="#quickstart">Start building</a>
              <a class="button" href="#packages">Explore packages</a>
            </div>
            <p class="prerelease"><strong>Prerelease</strong> · APIs may change before 1.0.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flow" aria-label="Dartpollo workflow: schema to typed response">
            <div class="flow-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="flow-node">
              <code>schema.graphql</code>
              <strong>Define the contract</strong>
              <p>Your GraphQL schema is the source of truth.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-node">
              <code>get_user.graphql</code>
              <strong>Write the operation</strong>
              <p>Queries stay readable and tool-friendly.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-node">
              <code>build_runner</code>
              <strong>Generate Dart types</strong>
              <p>Models, variables, fragments, and helpers.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-node">
              <code>DartpolloClient</code>
              <strong>Execute with confidence</strong>
              <p>Receive a typed response, optionally cached.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="docs-shell">
        <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
          <strong>On this page</strong>
          <a href="#quickstart">Quickstart</a>
          <a href="#packages">Packages</a>
          <a href="#client">Client</a>
          <a href="#caching">Caching</a>
          <a href="#configuration">Generator config</a>
        </aside>

        <article class="content">
          <section id="quickstart">
            <h2>From zero to typed query</h2>
            <p class="lead">Install two packages, map your schema to your operations, and let the generator create the Dart surface your app consumes.</p>
            <ol class="steps">
              <li>
                <h3>Add the runtime and generator</h3>
                <pre><code>dependencies:
  dartpollo: ^0.1.0-alpha.6

dev_dependencies:
  build_runner: ^2.10.0
  dartpollo_generator: ^0.1.0-alpha.6</code></pre>
              </li>
              <li>
                <h3>Connect schema and queries</h3>
                <p>Create <code>build.yaml</code> at your project root.</p>
                <pre><code>targets:
  $default:
    sources:
      - $package$
      - lib/**
      - schema.graphql
    builders:
      dartpollo_generator|dartpollo:
        options:
          schema_mapping:
            - schema: schema.graphql
              queries_glob: lib/**/*.graphql</code></pre>
              </li>
              <li>
                <h3>Generate the Dart types</h3>
                <pre><code>dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs</code></pre>
              </li>
              <li>
                <h3>Execute the generated query</h3>
                <pre><code>import 'package:dartpollo/dartpollo.dart';

final client = DartpolloClient(
  'https://api.example.com/graphql',
);

final response = await client.execute(GetUserQuery());
print(response.data);

client.dispose();</code></pre>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </section>

          <section id="packages">
            <h2>Three packages, one contract</h2>
            <p>The workspace separates runtime code from build-time tooling while sharing the types that keep both sides aligned.</p>
            <div class="package-map">
              <div class="package">
                <a href="https://pub.dev/packages/dartpollo">dartpollo ↗</a>
                <p>The runtime client: typed execution, streaming, cancellation, link composition, and cache stores.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="package">
                <a href="https://pub.dev/packages/dartpollo_generator">generator ↗</a>
                <p>The build-time generator for queries, response models, inputs, enums, and fragments.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="package">
                <a href="https://pub.dev/packages/dartpollo_annotation">annotation ↗</a>
                <p>The shared contract. It arrives transitively, so most applications do not add it directly.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="client">
            <h2>Use the client you need</h2>
            <p><code>DartpolloClient</code> is the direct path. Supply an endpoint, optional default headers or a custom Dio client, and execute generated query objects.</p>
            <pre><code>final client = DartpolloClient(
  'https://api.example.com/graphql',
  defaultHeaders: &#123;'Authorization': 'Bearer $token'&#125;,
  useGETForQueries: true,
);

final cancelToken = CancelToken();
final response = await client.execute(
  GetUserQuery(),
  context: Context().withCancelToken(cancelToken),
);</code></pre>
            <div class="callout">
              <strong>Bring your own link chain</strong>
              <p>Use <code>DartpolloClient.fromLink</code> when your transport needs deduplication, custom middleware, or an existing <code>gql_link</code> composition.</p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="caching">
            <h2>Caching stays explicit</h2>
            <p>Create <code>DartpolloCachedClient</code> when the application benefits from caching. Choose an in-memory store or persistent Hive storage, then override policy and TTL per request.</p>
            <pre><code>final client = DartpolloCachedClient(
  'https://api.example.com/graphql',
  cacheStore: InMemoryCacheStore(maxSize: 100),
  defaultCachePolicy: CachePolicy.cacheFirst,
  defaultCacheTtl: Duration(minutes: 5),
);

final response = await client.execute(
  GetUserQuery(),
  context: Context().cacheAndNetwork(),
);</code></pre>
            <table class="policy-table">
              <thead><tr><th>Policy</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>cacheFirst</code></td><td>Use a valid cached response; otherwise request the network.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>networkFirst</code></td><td>Try the network, falling back to cache when necessary.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>cacheOnly</code></td><td>Read locally without making a network request.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>networkOnly</code></td><td>Skip the cache and fetch fresh data.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>cacheAndNetwork</code></td><td>Stream cached data first, followed by the network response.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </section>

          <section id="configuration">
            <h2>Shape generated output</h2>
            <p>Generator options live under <code>dartpollo_generator|dartpollo</code> in <code>build.yaml</code>. Start with defaults and configure only what your schema needs.</p>
            <pre><code>options:
  optimize_document_nodes: true
  scalar_mapping:
    - graphql_type: DateTime
      dart_type:
        name: DateTime
    - graphql_type: JSON
      dart_type:
        name: Map&lt;String, dynamic&gt;
  schema_mapping:
    - schema: schema.graphql
      queries_glob: lib/**/*.graphql
      naming_scheme: pathedWithTypes
      append_type_name: false</code></pre>
            <p>Multiple schema mappings, shared fragment globs, custom scalar imports, enum conversion, naming schemes, and generated-file lint ignores are supported.</p>
            <div class="next">
              <a href="https://github.com/dwikyhardi/dartpollo/tree/main/packages/dartpollo/example">Browse examples ↗</a>
              <a href="https://github.com/dwikyhardi/dartpollo/issues">Report an issue ↗</a>
            </div>
          </section>
        </article>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <div class="footer-inner">
        <span>Dartpollo is available under the MIT License.</span>
        <span>Built for Dart and Flutter developers.</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
